@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{markdown-mode-extras.el} extends @samp{markdown-mode} with commands for
clipboard conversion@comma{} section manipulation@comma{} and link editing.  Much of
the package revolves around interoperability between Markdown and Org
mode@comma{} using Pandoc as the conversion engine.  If you frequently copy
content between Org and Markdown files@comma{} or paste formatted text from
the web into a Markdown buffer@comma{} these commands save considerable
manual reformatting.

The main capabilities are:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Clipboard conversion}: paste clipboard content while converting
between Org@comma{} Markdown@comma{} and HTML formats via Pandoc
(@ref{Clipboard conversion, , Clipboard conversion}).
@item
@strong{Section operations}: extract or copy the body of the current
Markdown section (@ref{Section operations, , Section operations}).
@item
@strong{Link editing}: strip the URL from a Markdown link@comma{} keeping only the
description text (@ref{Link editing, , Link editing}).
@item
@strong{Table alignment}: realign every pipe table in the buffer so column
separators line up (@ref{Table alignment, , Table alignment}).
@end itemize

